---
import ShellLayout from "../layouts/ShellLayout.astro";
import ScaffoldBanner from "../components/ScaffoldBanner.astro";
---
<ShellLayout title="About — Neoplastix" current="about">
  <ScaffoldBanner seat={3} handle="medinaxd29" title="Wave A scaffold" />
  <article class="prose about-story">
    <header data-scene class="about-scene">
      <p class="about-epigraph" data-speed="0.55">
        <q>
          La Plastique nouvelle met ses rapports en équilibre esthétique et
          exprime par là l'harmonie nouvelle.
        </q>
      </p>
      <p class="about-cite" data-speed="0.7">
        <cite>
          <i>Le Néoplasticisme</i>. Paris: Éditions de l'Effort Moderne (Léonce
          Rosenberg), 1920.
        </cite>
      </p>
      <h1 data-speed="1">About the study</h1>
      <p class="lede" data-speed="1">
        Seven short scenes: from a painting’s ratios to a print you can hold.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section data-scene class="about-scene" id="scene-measure">
      <div class="about-layer about-layer--bg" data-speed="0.4" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2 data-speed="1">1. A painting is measured</h2>
      <p data-speed="0.95">
        An instructor records the original canvas size, then places grid points,
        coloured rectangles and explicit black lines on a named reproduction.
        Those numbers live in immutable <code>work.yml</code> — never invented
        proportions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-scene class="about-scene" id="scene-ratios">
      <div class="about-layer about-layer--bg" data-speed="0.35" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2 data-speed="1">2. Geometry becomes ratios</h2>
      <p data-speed="0.95">
        Point positions and line thicknesses are normalized. Adjacent boundary
        deltas become track weights. The same arithmetic feeds CSS Grid and SVG.
        Classical prior art for this representation is Andrzejewski et al.
        (2010) on neoplastic structure — geometry only, not authenticity scoring.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-scene class="about-scene" id="scene-render">
      <div class="about-layer about-layer--bg" data-speed="0.45" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2 data-speed="1">3. Ratios become CSS and SVG</h2>
      <p data-speed="0.95">
        One derived render plan places planes under lines. The gallery draws that
        plan with CSS Grid; the forthcoming editor draws the same plan as SVG.
        Two skins, one spine.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-scene class="about-scene" id="scene-frame">
      <div class="about-layer about-layer--bg" data-speed="0.3" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2 data-speed="1">4. A frame changes</h2>
      <p data-speed="0.95">
        Corner-resize is free aspect. The pattern <strong>liquid-fills</strong>
        the new rectangle: relative fractions stay; absolute cells adapt. That is
        the joke — refactor Mondrian by changing the frame, not by dragging
        internal nodes (deferred past MVP).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-scene class="about-scene" id="scene-colour">
      <div class="about-layer about-layer--bg" data-speed="0.5" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2 data-speed="1">5. Colour becomes an angle</h2>
      <p data-speed="0.95">
        Chromatic roles rotate by θ in HSL; black, white and gray stay put. The
        directed Δ between two measured hues is invariant under that rotation —
        with the honest limit that HSL lightness is not perceived lightness.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-scene class="about-scene" id="scene-yours">
      <div class="about-layer about-layer--bg" data-speed="0.4" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2 data-speed="1">6. A pattern becomes yours</h2>
      <p data-speed="0.95">
        Catalog variations, hue and line-weight compose on the current fill.
        Preset buttons load build-time artefacts; they do not call a server.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-scene class="about-scene" id="scene-print">
      <div class="about-layer about-layer--bg" data-speed="0.35" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2 data-speed="1">7. The screen returns to paper</h2>
      <p data-speed="0.95">
        Save as a short recipe URL, SVG, HTML, CSV or PNG. Print uses physical
        presets (stickers first). Millimetre claims wait on calibration.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <script>
    import "../scripts/about-parallax.js";
  </script>
</ShellLayout>

<style>
  .about-story {
    max-width: 40rem;
  }
  .about-epigraph q {
    quotes: "«" "»";
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .about-cite {
    color: var(--mp-color-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .about-scene {
    position: relative;
    padding: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    isolation: isolate;
  }
  .about-layer--bg {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 10% -8% auto auto;
    width: 7rem;
    height: 7rem;
    background: linear-gradient(
      135deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--mp-role-red) 35%, transparent),
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--mp-role-blue) 25%, transparent)
    );
    z-index: -1;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .about-layer--bg {
      opacity: 0.35;
    }
  }
</style>
